From c76a9aaed4249fc16b1799163e55cf1f2485db6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 08:11:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rework trip detection into a speed+duration+distance state
 machine
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the single-speed-threshold trip start/stop logic with a proper
state machine: idle -> start_candidate -> active -> stop_candidate,
with stop_candidate able to fall back to active if the vehicle moves
again before the stop window elapses. A trip only confirms once speed,
sustained duration, and distance travelled all agree (not speed alone),
and only ends once the vehicle has been genuinely stationary (speed +
GPS displacement) for a sustained window, not just briefly slow.

- New src/config/tripDetectionConfig.ts: single source of truth for every
  trip-detection threshold (start/stop speed, duration, distance, GPS
  quality gates, and waypoint/progress write cadence) — nothing in
  autoTripEngine.ts hardcodes a tunable value anymore.
- autoTripEngine.ts: full state-machine rewrite. A confirmed trip's
  start time/location backdate to when movement actually began, and the
  distance/time accumulated during the candidate window carries into the
  trip rather than being discarded.
- autoTripStorage.ts: AutoTripState gains an explicit `phase` field and
  the candidate-window bookkeeping needed to support it; getAutoTripState
  merges over the empty-state defaults so an old persisted state (missing
  new fields) doesn't break on upgrade.
- Battery/data usage: trip_waypoints rows and the live in-progress
  vehicle_trips update are now throttled by time+distance/time
  respectively instead of writing on every ~5s GPS fix.

No changes to AI Inspection or any other feature; only these four files
touched.
